    <string-array name="weather_bio_pressure_text">
        <item>Stable pressure, no weather-sensitivity effects expected.</item>
        <item>Slight pressure change. Very sensitive people may notice mild tiredness.</item>
        <item>Noticeable pressure change. Headaches, irritability or poor concentration are possible for weather-sensitive people.</item>
        <item>Strong pressure change. Weather sensitivity likely: migraine, joint pain or circulation problems are possible. Plan rest breaks.</item>
        <item>Extreme pressure change. Physically demanding, especially for chronically ill, elderly or weather-sensitive people. Reduce exertion.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="weather_bio_humidity_text">
        <item>Comfortably dry, no mugginess effect.</item>
        <item>Slightly humid, comfortable.</item>
        <item>Noticeably muggy. Sweating cools less effectively, performance during activity is slightly reduced.</item>
        <item>Clearly muggy. Circulation is under more strain. Drink enough and move activity to cooler hours.</item>
        <item>Extremely muggy. Heat exhaustion possible. Strongly limit activity, drink a lot, seek shade.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="weather_bio_heat_text">
        <item>Pleasant warmth, no heat stress.</item>
        <item>Slight heat stress possible during sustained physical activity.</item>
        <item>Moderate heat stress. Drink plenty and avoid midday heat.</item>
        <item>Strong heat stress. Avoid intense activity, stay in the shade, drink enough.</item>
        <item>Extreme heat stress. Risk of heat stroke. Reduce activity to a minimum.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="weather_bio_cold_text">
        <item>Cool, but no critical cold stress.</item>
        <item>Slight cold stress. Dress warmly.</item>
        <item>Noticeable cold stress. Warm clothing needed, protect hands, head and feet.</item>
        <item>Strong cold stress. Frostbite risk in wind without protective clothing. Limit time outdoors.</item>
        <item>Extreme cold. Frostbite on bare skin is possible within minutes.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="weather_bio_cape_text">
        <item>Low thunderstorm potential, no effect on well-being.</item>
        <item>Elevated thunderstorm potential. Atmospheric instability can increase restlessness and discomfort.</item>
        <item>High thunderstorm potential. Mood swings and circulation complaints are possible.</item>
    </string-array>
